  "question": {
    "text": "A rectangular block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> attached to a horizontal spiral spring executes simple harmonic motion of amplitude <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;and time period <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>. The maximum force exerted by spring on block is ___ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "20",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>By Newton&#39;s second law,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></math>.</p><p>The maximum acceleration for a SHM is given by&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>The time period is given by&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mi>&#969;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>rad</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Thus, the maximum acceleration from equation (i)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>The maximum force is&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
